## Unicorn (30 words)
> A unicorn is a mythical horse-like creature with a single pointed horn on its forehead, often symbolizing purity, rarity, and magic across many cultures and legends.

## Irish History (2 sentences)
Ireland's history stretches from Mesolithic hunter-gatherers and Celtic Gaelic culture through Viking raids, the Norman invasion of 1169, and more than 800 years of English and British political involvement, including the Tudor conquest, the Plantations, and the Penal Laws. After the 1798 rebellion, the Great Famine of 1845, and the 1916 Easter Rising, most of Ireland gained independence as the Irish Free State in 1922 after the War of Independence, while the six northeastern counties remained in the United Kingdom as Northern Ireland, later wracked by the Troubles until the 1998 Good Friday Agreement brought peace.
